    "rich_text_3w4MYb": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_qPjMM7": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Foam Tape Resistance Capabilities: Open Vs. Closed",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_YnDQqn": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>While open cell foam tapes are resistant to oxygen and have a high degree of flexibility and dexterity, they don’t offer much in terms of resistance to water or moisture vapors. Closed cell foam tape offers a variety of beneficial features, such as excellent leak resistance, good soundproofing and shock capabilities, and high resistances to heat, moisture, and vapors.</p>",
            "text_size": "text-base",
            "text_line_limit": "none",
            "button_style": "btn--underline",
            "button_icon": "none"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_qPjMM7",
        "text_YnDQqn"
      ],
